யுடை","gloss":"very great"}],"gloss":"very great"},{"surface":"பரிசில்","parts":[{"text":"பரிசில்","lemma":"பரிசில்","gloss":"gift"}],"gloss":"gift"},{"surface":"தருகம்","parts":[{"text":"தருகம்","lemma":"தரு","gloss":"let us receive"}],"gloss":"let us receive"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"எழுமதி","parts":[{"text":"எழுமதி","lemma":"எழு","gloss":"rise up"}],"gloss":"rise up"},{"surface":"நெஞ்சே","parts":[{"text":"நெஞ்சே","lemma":"நெஞ்சு","gloss":"O heart"}],"gloss":"O heart"},{"surface":"துணிபு","parts":[{"text":"துணிபு","lemma":"துணிபு","gloss":"resolve"}],"gloss":"resolve"},{"surface":"முந்துறுத்தே","parts":[{"text":"முந்துறுத்தே","lemma":"முந்துறுத்து","gloss":"placing in front"}],"gloss":"placing in front"}]}],"literal":"May you live long! saying so, I approached the tall gate / and stood singing on a day of hunger, / like a thick shade in the summer season, / at the ear of the strong man who knows no falsehood, / the sown poem has ripened well, so saying / the hope we had with desire having become ruined, / like a cooked pot yielding only heat, / without saying 'let the pitiable ones themselves eat', / the virtueless God of Death, unjustly resolving, / as fate burned them, the stricken women / scattered their broken bangles like banana flowers, / while wise kinsmen and prize-seekers lamented, / in the wasteland overgrown with cactus, / the young hero with a white spear has gone and died. / Let that be without grief there! On the high mountain, / if the tiger misses the elephant prey it watched and stalked, / it will not watch and stalk a rat. Like the water rushing into the sea with abundant waves, / going with a rushing sound, / let us receive a very great gift. / Rise up, O heart, placing resolve in front!","translation":"I approached his tall gate, wishing him a long life, and stood singing on a day of deep hunger. He was like a thick, cooling shade in the heat of summer. I hoped that the poem I sowed in the ears of that strong man who never failed his word had ripened well. But that hope was ruined. Like a cooking pot that yields only heat when there is no food, the virtueless God of Death, acting unjustly, took him away without letting him say, 'Let these poor people eat.' As fate burned them, his grieving women broke and scattered their bangles, looking like banana flowers, while his wise kinsmen and prize-seekers lamented. In the dry wasteland overgrown with cactus, the young hero of the white spear has gone and died. Let us not grieve over that! A tiger on a high mountain, if it misses the elephant prey it stalked, will never stoop to hunt a rat. Like the swift waters rushing with a roar into the wave-filled sea, let us go and receive a great gift elsewhere. Rise up, O my heart, with determination leading the way!","modern":"நெடுங்காலம் வாழ்க என்று கூறி, நான் அவனது பெரிய வாயிலை அணுகி, பசியோடு பாடி நின்றேன். கோடைக் காலத்தில் குளிர்ந்த நிழல் போல விளங்கியவனும், பொய் கூறாதவனுமாகிய அந்த வலிமைமிக்க வள்ளலின் காதுகளில் நான் பாடிய பாடல் நல்ல பயனைத் தரும் என்று நம்பியிருந்தேன். ஆனால், அந்த நம்பிக்கை வீணாயிற்று. உணவில்லாத வெற்றுப் பானை வெறும் வெப்பத்தை மட்டும் தருவது போல, இரக்கமில்லாத கூற்றுவன் முறைதவறி அவனது உயிரைக் கவர்ந்து சென்றான். 'இந்த ஏழைகள் பசி தீர உண்ணட்டும்' என்று அவன் கூறுவதற்கும் வழியில்லாமல் போயிற்று. ஊழ்வினை வருத்த, அவனது மகளிர் அழுது புலம்பி, வாழைப்பூப் போன்ற தங்கள் வளையல்களை உடைத்துச் சிதறினர். அறிவுடைய சுற்றத்தாரும் பரிசில் பெறுவோரும் இரங்கி அழ, கள்ளிச் செடிகள் நிறைந்த சுடுகாட்டில், வெள்வேல் ஏந்திய அந்த இளஞ்சிங்கமாகிய வெளிமான் இறந்துபட்டான். அது கிடக்கட்டும், அதற்காக நாம் வருந்த வேண்டாம். உயர்ந்த மலையில் வாழும் புலி, தான் குறிவைத்த யானை தப்பியோடினாலும், எலியைப் பிடிக்க முயலாது. அதுபோல, அலைகள் நிறைந்த கடலில் பாயும் ஆற்று நீரைப் போல, நாம் விரைந்து சென்று வேறொருவரிடம் தகுந்த பரிசிலைப் பெறுவோம். என் நெஞ்சமே! துணிவை முன்னிறுத்தி எழுந்து புறப்படு!","explanation":"The poet Peruñcittiraṉār laments the untimely death of the young chieftain Iḷaveḷimāṉ. He describes how he approached the patron's gate in deep hunger, hoping his poetic songs would bear fruit, only for death to snatch the generous leader away. The poet compares the tragic loss to an empty cooking pot that yields only heat instead of food, leaving the dependents and kinsmen in deep grief. The women break their bangles in mourning, and the hero is laid to rest in a desolate cremation ground overgrown with cactus. However, the poet rouses his own heart, using the powerful image of a tiger that, even if it misses an elephant, will never deign to hunt a rat. He resolves to seek another worthy patron with dignity, comparing their journey to a roaring river rushing to the sea.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.8],[0.8,1.2],[1.2,1.5],[1.5,2.0],[2.0,2.5],[2.5,2.9],[2.9,3.2],[3.2,3.3],[3.3,4.0],[4.0,4.54],[4.54,5.4],[5.4,5.86],[5.97,6.2],[6.2,7.2],[7.2,7.5],[7.5,7.9],[7.9,8.2],[8.2,9.8],[9.8,10.0],[10.12,10.6],[10.6,10.92],[11.0,11.3],[11.3,11.3],[11.3,11.9],[12.28,12.7],[12.7,13.1],[13.1,13.9],[13.9,14.1],[14.1,14.88],[15.0,15.0],[15.0,16.0],[16.0,16.3],[16.3,16.6],[16.6,16.9],[17.72,18.32],[18.32,18.42],[18.42,19.22],[19.22,19.62],[19.62,20.22],[20.22,20.22],[20.49,21.02],[21.02,21.42],[21.42,22.07],[22.07,22.72],[22.72,23.07],[23.07,23.42],[23.42,24.42],[24.42,24.52],[24.52,24.92],[24.92,25.62],[25.62,26.32],[26.32,26.62],[26.62,26.92],[26.92,26.92],[26.92,28.62],[28.62,28.62],[28.62,29.32],[29.32,29.5],[30.18,30.82],[30.82,30.98],[30.98,31.62],[31.72,31.82],[31.82,32.52],[32.52,33.24],[33.24,33.82],[33.82,34.52],[34.52,35.02],[35.76,36.66],[36.66,37.06],[37.06,37.36],[37.36,37.66],[37.66,37.96],[37.96,38.89],[38.89,39.36],[39.36,39.91],[39.91,40.16],[40.16,40.96],[40.96,41.36],[41.36,41.76],[41.76,41.96],[41.96,42.56],[42.96,43.36],[43.36,43.66]],"female":[[0.0,0.9],[0.9,1.3],[1.3,1.6],[1.6,2.1],[2.1,2.73],[2.73,3.4],[3.4,3.7],[3.7,3.8],[3.8,4.44],[4.6,5.16],[5.16,6.0],[6.0,6.51],[6.64,6.9],[6.9,8.0],[8.0,8.3],[8.3,8.9],[8.9,9.2],[9.2,10.8],[10.8,11.0],[11.14,11.7],[11.7,12.18],[12.3,12.6],[12.6,13.08],[13